{"id": "EUVD-2026-108758", "enisaUuid": "3ae5a49c-f5b8-3b18-be17-9138ab09164f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet: use the local P2P device on metadata allocation failure\n\nnvmet_req_alloc_p2pmem_sgls() assigns req->p2p_dev only after the data\nand metadata SGL allocations succeed. If the data allocation succeeds\nbut the metadata allocation fails, out_free_sg passes req->p2p_dev to\npci_p2pmem_free_sgl() before that assignment has taken place.\n\nPass the local p2p_dev argument instead, so cleanup uses the same PCI\ndevice as the successful data allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c231142c4f4bb96836469eb276026ec55940093", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32f21607911a1f69c8f0f93a6c28fe6f8490aa98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce79a6c5cc1b8054ec8d3eba16adda4a36113438", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73bf0f9579633b531098a475e6e55c9316763aed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aa9c0f377a4de5e8fddce76b34ee4529639a1ff"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98964"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0061c352-bb15-3697-880d-8cb659d13d16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.43 <5.11"}, {"id": "006c2feb-0158-3b3d-8600-efa45c7087d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bcd9a0797d73eeff659582f23277e7ab6e5f18f3 <32f21607911a1f69c8f0f93a6c28fe6f8490aa98"}, {"id": "05e7460b-5733-3886-86b8-604408ff9385", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bcd9a0797d73eeff659582f23277e7ab6e5f18f3 <73bf0f9579633b531098a475e6e55c9316763aed"}, {"id": "06ad3eb0-98e3-33be-bb0a-5eed27e4d942", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bcd9a0797d73eeff659582f23277e7ab6e5f18f3 <3c231142c4f4bb96836469eb276026ec55940093"}, {"id": "1156f5e6-e